illumos: libstdc++ must use the thread-local errno.

Without _TS_ERRNO (or _REENTRANT), illumos <errno.h> makes errno a global int.
libstdc++ is built without either, so std::filesystem reads the global errno
after a failing lstat() in a thread, gets 0, and throws "Error 0" instead of
returning not_found. MEASURED: our gcc-14.3.0-lib had 86 references to the
global errno@SUNW_0.7 and 22 to ___errno; OpenIndiana's libstdc++ has 1 and 141.
An 8-thread symlink_status() probe on a missing path threw 16000/16000; nix's
optimise-store hit it on every multi-path substitution.

Taken verbatim from OpenIndiana oi-userland components/developer/gcc-14/
patches/0032-libstdc-must-use-thread-local-errno.patch (Andy Fiddaman, OmniOS),
with the a/ b/ prefixes normalised for patch -p1.

From 09e1d8748f9321bae39811e0f51683d330098cf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Fiddaman <omnios@citrus-it.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 31 Aug 2021 21:40:48 +0000
Subject: libstdc++ must use thread-local errno

---
 libstdc++-v3/configure    | 6 ++++++
 libstdc++-v3/configure.ac | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/libstdc++-v3/configure
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/configure
@@ -55105,6 +55105,12 @@
 tmake_file="${tmake_file_}"
 
 
+case "${target}" in *-*-solaris2*)
+	EXTRA_CFLAGS="$EXTRA_CFLAGS -D_TS_ERRNO"
+	EXTRA_CXX_FLAGS="$EXTRA_CXX_FLAGS -D_TS_ERRNO"
+esac
+
+
 # Add CET specific flags if Intel CET is enabled.
  # Check whether --enable-cet was given.
 if test "${enable_cet+set}" = set; then :
--- a/libstdc++-v3/configure.ac
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/configure.ac
@@ -658,6 +658,11 @@
 tmake_file="${tmake_file_}"
 AC_SUBST(tmake_file)
 
+case "${target}" in *-*-solaris2*)
+	EXTRA_CFLAGS="$EXTRA_CFLAGS -D_TS_ERRNO"
+	EXTRA_CXX_FLAGS="$EXTRA_CXX_FLAGS -D_TS_ERRNO"
+esac
+
 # Add CET specific flags if Intel CET is enabled.
 GCC_CET_FLAGS(CET_FLAGS)
 EXTRA_CXX_FLAGS="$EXTRA_CXX_FLAGS $CET_FLAGS"
